<title>SWITZERLAND: FIGURE SKATING-STOJKO WINS WORLD MEN'S GOLD MEDAL.</title>
<headline>FIGURE SKATING-STOJKO WINS WORLD MEN'S GOLD MEDAL.</headline>
<dateline>LAUSANNE, Switzerland 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Elvis Stojko of Canada won the gold medal in the men's event at the world figure skating championships on Thursday.</p>
<p>American Todd Eldredge won the silver medal for second place and Russian Alexei Yagudin took the bronze.</p>
<p>Olympic champion Alexei Urmanov of Russia withdrew with an injury.</p>
</text>
